// SPEC O11's table (A:1252) and the EN0710 mapping (A:1289), one body per row; the
// loans are shared or exclusive by N3 rule (a) alone, so the codes do not depend on
// the argument modes of plan d.7.
// Source:
//   e706() { let x = 1; const r = &x; x = 2; console.log(*r); }       // EN0706 at `x = 2`
//   e707() { let x = 12; const y = &x; x = 3; *y = 13; }              // EN0707 at `x = 3` (O7)
//   e708() { let x = 12; const y = &x; const v = x; *y = 13; }        // EN0708 at `x` (O7)
//   e709(v: i64[]) { const r = &v; const t = v; console.log(*r); }    // EN0709 at `v`
//   e712() { const s = first(&pair()); console.log(*s); }             // EN0712 where the temporary ends (S:949)
//   g10(): &i64 { const s = 1; return &s; }                          // EN0710 at `&s` (G10)
//   guard() { const x = 1; { const g = new Guard { r: &x }; } }      // compiles: a destructor runs on `g`
//   guarded() { let x = 1; const g = new Guard { r: &x }; x = 2; }    // EN0706: the scope-end drop runs `g`'s destructor
//   plain() { let x = 1; const t = new Tagged { r: &x }; x = 2; }     // compiles: no destructor, `t` is dead
// Shapes: reference locals' copies as reborrows (A:935), `console.log` as a form on a
// reborrow (c.7 D19), a statement temporary borrowed `[temp-arg]` and ended at the
// statement (c.3, c.5), `return &s` into `_0` then the scope end (c.9), a named
// form (c.10) and the scope-end `drop` of a value with a destructor (c.3).
